scope: |
  v3 execution performance. Measured 2026-08-09 on a contended host: exec runs
  bench/corpus/arith-loop.ssc in 226.99 ms against v1's 0.244 (~930x) and list-fold in
  60.06 against 0.0062 (~9700x). Static cause of the second: Exec$.invoke is 13415
  bytecodes, over HotSpot's DontCompileHugeMethods=8000, so it is never JIT-compiled.

  NOT a port of v1's JIT: v1 spent ~10k lines building a register machine out of a
  scalameta tree and v3's IR already is one. Spec: specs/ssc3-jit.md. Tiers J0 (executor
  hygiene) and J1 (the NumKind specializer + Invoke name->id) first; the host-bytecode
  backend behind a by-name seam is a separate decision after the numbers.

  Exec.scala WAS excluded while ssc3-cps-split held it; that claim released in 304f33ec0
  and no other claim declares the file, so J1b (step dispatches on kind) and J0 (split
  invoke, materialize the const pool, Array[Instr]) are now in scope.
next: write specs/ssc3-jit.md, plan J0..J3 into v3/SPRINT.md, then build the gate before the feature
